// FILE: index_law_v1.law
/*******************************************************************************
 *                           AVIS.ARTIFACT HEADER
 * TYPE: LAW
 * CLASS: INDEX-LAW
 * NAME: INDEX-LAW-V1
 * VERSION: 1.00
 * ROLE: Cross-Reference Rules for AVIS Laws
 * ENGINE: AVIS-2026 / AIFVS-MODE
 * ORIGIN: /mercwar01/law/index_law_v1.law
 *******************************************************************************
 * [PURPOSE]
 * Define how governance artifacts reference, cite, and interlink with each
 * other within the AVIS ecosystem.
 *
 * [INDEX PRINCIPLES]
 * 1. Explicit Reference:
 *    Laws must reference other laws by NAME and VERSION.
 *
 * 2. Non-Ambiguity:
 *    References must not rely on context or inference.
 *
 * 3. Stability:
 *    References should remain valid across versions unless explicitly updated.
 *
 * [REFERENCE FORMAT]
 * A reference must include:
 *   - LAW-NAME
 *   - VERSION
 *   - OPTIONAL: SECTION label
 *
 * Example:
 *   REF: MODULE-LAW-V1 / SECTION: MODULE PRINCIPLES
 *
 * [REFERENCE TYPES]
 * - HARD REF: Required dependency.
 * - SOFT REF: Optional or contextual dependency.
 * - META REF: Reference to a category (e.g., “all FORGING-COVENANT laws”).
 *
 * [UPDATE RULES]
 * - When a referenced law is updated, dependent laws must specify whether
 *   they adopt the new version or remain bound to the previous one.
 *
 * [COMPLIANCE]
 * All governance artifacts must follow this law to maintain clarity and
 * interoperability across the AVIS legal layer.
 *******************************************************************************
 * [END AVIS.ARTIFACT]
 *******************************************************************************/
